 "question": "B. Is this measure already running in South Ostrobothnia wellbeing services county (or in the Tays university hospital area that treats its patients)?\nA. Does recent evidence support the size of effect we assume: does this measure shorten the time from first symptom to treatment start for lung cancer patients, and by how much?\nMeasure: Nurse navigator for every suspected lung cancer. A named nurse books and chases every test, calls the patient, prepares the MDT and removes waiting between steps from referral to first treatment.",
 "area_id": "16",
 "verdict": "mixed",
 "effect_check": "weaker",
 "effect_summary_en": "A 2026 scoping review of 13 studies found navigation was consistently associated with faster first treatment, but the abstract gives no pooled number of days saved and nothing specific to lung cancer.",
 "supported_en": "A 2026 scoping review of 13 studies in the Japan Journal of Nursing Science found patient navigation consistently associated with faster first treatment.",
 "not_supported_en": "The review gives no difference against usual care, so it does not show our assumed 15 % (0–30 %) cut in waiting time.",
