 "summary_en": "The Hyvaep pages on lung disease and cancer services and the Pirha/Tays lung cancer pages name doctors, a specialist meeting, rehabilitation counsellors and a doctor–nurse pair at the Tays lung clinic, but none describes a nurse who books and chases every test for each suspected lung cancer. Hyvaep's lung clinic says lung cancer found there is treated elsewhere case by case, and Hyvaep's cancer clinic says radiotherapy is mainly given with Vaasa central hospital. A 2026 scoping review of 13 studies found navigation consistently associated with faster first treatment, without a pooled number of days saved.",
 "unanswered_en": "We found no page from Hyvaep or Tays on a lung cancer nurse coordinator, project or pilot, and no study that measures how many days a navigator saves for lung cancer patients.",
